# Vibe-Coding Prompt Pack — MLR RuleOps Demo App

**How to use:** paste **Prompt 1** into Google AI Studio / Lovable / v0 / Bolt / Cursor as a single message. Then use the follow-up prompts to refine. Prompt 1 is self-contained — it includes the data seed, the logic rules, and the non-negotiables.

---

## PROMPT 1 — Master build prompt (paste this first)

````
Build a single-page web application called "MLR RuleOps" — a demo of an AI-assisted
change-management platform for a pharmaceutical MLR (Medical/Legal/Regulatory) rules engine.

## CONTEXT
Pharma companies run an "AI Assisted Review" gate that checks promotional content against
compliance rules before formal MLR review. Business users file tickets asking to change those
rules (e.g. "update the US cardiovascular disclaimer to cite the 2026 trial and drop the 2020
study"). Today admins do this by hand and it takes 20-36 days. This app shows AI parsing the
ticket, finding the right rule, drafting the change, regression-testing it, and STOPPING for
human approval before deploying.

## TECH
- React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS. Single-page app with client-side routing.
- No backend. All state in memory (React context or Zustand). Seed data hard-coded as JSON.
- Dark theme: background #0E1726, panels #16223A, accent gold #C9A34E, text #FFFFFF / #CADCFC.
- Font: Georgia for headings, system sans for body. Professional, enterprise, uncluttered.

## SCREENS (exactly 4 — do not add more)
1. /tickets — Ticket Queue
2. /workspace/:ticketId — Change Workspace (AI parse → rule discovery → diff)
3. /workspace/:ticketId#test — Test & Risk panel (revealed on same page after running pipeline)
4. /approval/:changeId and /audit/:changeId — HITL approval + audit trail

Left sidebar nav with only: Tickets · Change Workspace · Approvals · Audit.
Footer on every screen: "Illustrative / synthetic data — not real regulatory content".

### SCREEN 1 — Ticket Queue
Table of tickets: Ticket ID, Source, Title, Market, Brand, Change Type, Risk (coloured chip:
LOW green / MEDIUM amber / HIGH red / CRITICAL dark red), Stage, Age.
Search box + Stage filter + Risk filter. Clicking a row opens /workspace/:ticketId.
Include a "Reset demo" button that returns all tickets to stage RECEIVED.

### SCREEN 2 — Change Workspace
Header shows ticket ID + title and a "▶ Run pipeline" button.
When clicked, reveal four panels IN SEQUENCE with ~600ms delay between each:

Panel A "Original request" — the raw ticket text + requester + priority.

Panel B "AI interpretation" — a small table: Intent, Market, Brand, Category, and a large
confidence percentage (e.g. 98%).

Panel C "Rule discovery & disambiguation" — THE MOST IMPORTANT PANEL.
Show a table of AT LEAST 3 candidate rules with columns: Rule ID, Layer, Scope, Match %,
Status. Exactly one row is highlighted and labelled SELECTED; the others are labelled
"overridden" or "less specific". Below the table show a reasoning box:
"Why this rule: exact US market + Drug A brand + Cardiovascular + Disclaimer match.
Market-level rule overridden by the more specific Market-Brand rule."
NEVER show only a single matched rule — always show the candidates it rejected.

Panel D "Proposed change — before / after" — render the disclaimer as READABLE PROSE with
the removed text in red with strikethrough and the added text in green highlight.
DO NOT show raw config tokens like REMOVE_REFERENCE "CIT-2020-001". A human must be able to
read the sentence. Show pills underneath: "v4 → v5 (draft)", "syntax valid ✓",
"dependencies intact ✓".

Footer button: "Run validation & tests →" which reveals Screen 3 content below.

### SCREEN 3 — Test & Risk (same route, anchor #test)
Row of 5 stat cards: Assets affected 34 | Reviews replayed 48 | Unchanged 46 |
Changed as expected 2 | Broken 0 (render "Broken 0" in green, large).

Then a "Regression detail" table: Asset, Market/Brand, Before, After, Note.
CRITICAL: one row (CNT-003) must show Before=FAIL → After=PASS, highlighted, with the note
"Now passes — 2026 citation is live". This proves the change is correct, not just valid.
Other rows stay PASS→PASS unchanged.

Then two cards: "Risk assessment" (shows the computed risk chip + reason) and
"Required gate" (shows the gate text + a "Send for approval →" button).
If Broken > 0, disable the approval button.

### SCREEN 4 — Approval & Audit
Top banner (amber/gold): "⏸ Pipeline halted. This change will NOT deploy until an authorised
MLR Admin approves it. No LLM writes to production."

Cards: "Change summary" (rule, version v4→v5, risk chip, test result, requester) and
"Current live rule (input transparency)" showing the production value before approval, with a
"view full rule JSON" expander.

"Approver action" card: a REQUIRED free-text "Approval rationale" field. The
"✓ Approve & deploy" button stays DISABLED until rationale is non-empty. Also
"Request changes" and "Reject" secondary buttons.

"Audit trail (append-only)" table: Time, Actor, Action, Detail. Rows:
TICKET_RECEIVED (system) → INTENT_PARSED (AI, conf 98%) → RULE_SELECTED (AI, 2 candidates
rejected) → REGRESSION_PASSED (48 replayed, 0 broken). After the user clicks Approve, APPEND
two new rows live: APPROVED (Priya Shah, with her typed rationale) and DEPLOYED (system,
v4 → v5). Never delete rows.
Include a "↺ Rollback to v4" button that appends a ROLLED_BACK audit row.

## CONDITIONAL STATES (implement all three)
State A — Disambiguation gate: if match confidence < 90% OR two candidates are within 10% of
each other, show an amber banner "⚠ Ambiguous request — market not specified" and require the
user to click "select" on one of the candidate rules before the pipeline continues.

State B — Critical dual approval: if riskTier is CRITICAL, the approval screen shows TWO
approver rows (Dr. M. Reid / Scientific — PENDING, and Priya Shah / MLR Admin — SIGNED), a
reference to "RMCB-SOP-114", and the deploy button is DISABLED and reads
"Deploy — blocked (1 of 2 signed)".

State C — Guardrail block: if the request targets a safety/ISI field AND the intent is to
weaken/soften/remove, do NOT generate a draft. Show a red banner "⛔ Change refused. Request
would weaken approved safety language." plus "Action: escalated to RMCB". Approve is unavailable.

## RISK → GATE LOGIC (hard-code this)
LOW      = text-string change, single market, no safety field   → Single approval
MEDIUM   = text-string change with market-wide blast radius      → Single approval + rationale
HIGH     = restricted term or claim wording                      → Approval + impact report
CRITICAL = business-logic/routing change or scientific value     → Dual approval + RMCB, deploy blocked

## SEED DATA (use exactly these tickets)
TKT-1001 | ServiceNow | "Update the US cardiovascular disclaimer for Drug A to include the new
  2026 clinical trial citation and remove reference to the 2020 study." | US | Drug A |
  Text string | LOW | confidence 98% | target RULE-US-DRUGA-CV-014
TKT-1006 | Jira | "Add a routing rule: if Drug X is mentioned in Japan promotional material,
  require both RA and Scientific reviewer sign-off." | JP | Drug X | Business logic | CRITICAL
TKT-1009 | Jira | "Reword the US patient safety statement to soften the ocular adverse-reaction
  warning tone." | US | Drug B | Text string | HIGH | → triggers guardrail block
TKT-1004 | ServiceNow | "Update the disclaimer to add the 2026 citation." | — | Drug A |
  Text string | MEDIUM | confidence 62% | → triggers disambiguation gate
TKT-1016 | ServiceNow | "Roll back the US disclaimer to the version before the 2026 citation
  change." | US | Drug A | Rollback | MEDIUM

Candidate rules for TKT-1001:
  RULE-US-DRUGA-CV-014 | Market-Brand | US · Drug A · Cardiovascular | 98% | SELECTED
  RULE-US-CV-002       | Market       | US · all brands              | 71% | overridden
  RULE-DRUGA-BASE-007  | Brand        | Global · Drug A              | 64% | less specific

Rule content before: "Drug A is indicated to reduce cardiovascular risk in appropriate adults.
(Smith et al., 2020, CV-OUTCOMES) Please see full Prescribing Information."
Rule content after: same sentence but "(Smith et al., 2020, CV-OUTCOMES)" removed and
"(Johnson et al., 2026, CV-OUTCOMES-2)" added.

Regression assets: CNT-003 (US/Drug A) FAIL→PASS [highlight]; CNT-001 (US/Drug A) PASS→PASS;
CNT-004 (DE/Drug A) PASS→PASS "DE rule untouched"; CNT-013 (US/Drug A) FAIL→FAIL "unrelated
superlative claim".

## NON-NEGOTIABLES
1. The pipeline MUST halt at AWAITING_APPROVAL. Never auto-deploy. Never show the golden
   ticket as already closed on load.
2. Rule discovery always shows ≥3 candidates with match % and an explicit selection reason.
3. The diff is human-readable prose, never config tokens.
4. The regression panel highlights the FAIL→PASS row and shows "Broken 0".
5. Approval requires a typed rationale.
6. Audit is append-only and updates live when the user approves.
7. Synthetic-data disclaimer visible on every screen.
8. Keep it to 4 screens — no settings, analytics, or admin pages.

Make it look like enterprise software a pharma compliance team would trust: calm, dense but
uncluttered, generous whitespace, no gradients, no emoji except the small status glyphs above.
````

